---
/**
 * Why the weeks run in this order.
 *
 * The four-week list on the page already says what happens; repeating it as a
 * flow would be decoration. What the list cannot show is the page's actual
 * argument — that design coming first is the thing that makes projects late —
 * so this contrasts the two orderings and marks the sign-off that separates
 * them. The failure row is deliberately drawn flat and grey: it is not a
 * competitor being sneered at, it is the order most projects fall into.
 */
const usual = [
  { step: 'Design first', note: 'Approved on placeholder text' },
  { step: 'Content, later', note: 'Waiting on the clinic for weeks' },
  { step: 'Launch, slipped', note: 'Words rushed to fit the design' },
];

const ours = [
  { step: 'Study', note: 'What patients here actually search' },
  { step: 'Words', note: 'Signed off before any visuals', gate: true },
  { step: 'Design', note: 'One pass, on your real content' },
  { step: 'Launch', note: 'Measured against the targets' },
];
---

<div class="grid gap-5">
  <div>
    <p class="label-mono mb-3 text-faint">How it usually goes</p>
    <ol class="flex list-none flex-col gap-2 p-0 sm:flex-row sm:items-stretch sm:gap-2.5">
      {usual.map((u) => (
        <li class="flex-1 rounded-xl border border-dashed border-line-strong bg-hairline-soft px-4 py-3">
          <p class="text-[14.5px] font-semibold text-muted">{u.step}</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-[12.5px] leading-[1.45] text-faint">{u.note}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div>
    <p class="label-mono mb-3 text-surgical">How we run it</p>
    <ol class="flex list-none flex-col gap-2 p-0 sm:flex-row sm:items-stretch sm:gap-2.5">
      {ours.map((o) => (
        <li
          class:list={[
            'flex-1 rounded-xl border px-4 py-3',
            o.gate ? 'border-surgical bg-surgical-tint' : 'border-line bg-canvas',
          ]}
        >
          <p class="text-[14.5px] font-semibold text-ink">{o.step}</p>
          <p class:list={['mt-1 text-[12.5px] leading-[1.45]', o.gate ? 'text-surgical' : 'text-muted']}>
            {o.note}
          </p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </div>
</div>
<p class="mt-5 text-[13.5px] leading-[1.55] text-muted">
  The sign-off in week two is the whole difference. Once the words are agreed,
  design decorates something real instead of hiding that it is missing.
</p>
